 "meta": {
  "schema": "cards-model-v7-narrative",
  "genre": "narrative",
  "note": "Narrative is the one genre in the portfolio where the language is PARADIGMATIC rather than syntagmatic. An essay or a letter moves through a sequence of rhetorical moves, one phrase per slot; a story picks three or four items from different word classes inside a single sentence. So the unit here is the ingredient, not the line: `recipe` gives the formula for a sentence at that stage, `ingredients` gives the classes to draw from, and `frames` gives sentence openers for learners who need the scaffold.",
  "gradeNote": "Every ingredient carries a `grade`: 1 = plain (safe, B1, what a learner reaches for unprompted), 2 = B2 core (the working range, and where most marks are won), 3 = ambitious (a reach, worth one or two per story, costly if overused). The grade is the teaching axis — walked -> hurried -> hurtled is the same choice point at three levels, and showing the ladder is what turns a word list into an upgrade. Where the other genres grade by REGISTER, narrative grades by VIVIDNESS.",
  "breakingChange": "Ingredients were plain strings and are now objects {w, grade}. Any page reading them needs `.w`. narrative-cards.html has not been updated."
 },
